#====================================================================
# E226 - Bound FFTW planning policy to target startup evidence
#====================================================================

id:                     E304
trigger_tool:           cmake|ctest|runtime
phase:                  configuration|testing|runtime
error_signature:        Mdrun.*\(Timeout\)|FFTW_MEASURE|Using [0-9]+ MPI thread

severity:               3
category:               fftw-runtime-planning
match_keywords:         FFTW_MEASURE, FFTW_ESTIMATE, GMX_DISABLE_FFTW_MEASURE, PME, CTest timeout, repeated process startup
title:                  Prevent exhaustive FFTW planning from consuming short target test budgets

root_cause:             A project-level no-measure option can reach the primary FFT wrapper but miss a direct multidimensional planner, leaving that path on FFTW_MEASURE during every fresh process startup; constrained targets then spend minutes planning before a tiny transform or simulation makes progress.
affected_scope:         CMake applications that repeatedly create FFTW plans in short-lived target processes, especially PME or multidimensional transforms on embedded AArch64 systems.
verification_cmd:       Bind the configure macro and final planner selection, then rerun the complete registered suite and require all tests plus package consumers to pass within the unchanged outer budget.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           evidence-bound-fftw-estimate
rec_description:        When target timing proves FFTW planning dominates startup, enable the conservative planning option and audit every direct FFT planner so the same policy reaches all FFTW_MEASURE selections while preserving transforms, tests, and result assertions.
rec_command:            Set the project's supported no-measure CMake option to ON, verify the generated macro and every direct planner flag, then rerun the full suite rather than only timed-out tests.
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-cmake-toolchain

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      persistent-fftw-wisdom
fallback_description:   If production throughput requires measured plans and the application supports it, generate and reuse target-bound FFTW wisdom with exact CPU and library identity.
fallback_command:       Persist only validated target wisdom and prove both first-run and reuse behavior.
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          runtime-configuration

forbid_1_pattern:       exclude.*Mdrun|ctest.*-E|increase.*timeout.*without.*timing
forbid_1_reason:        Removing tests or only increasing their timeout hides a repeated planning bottleneck without proving simulation correctness.
forbid_1_consequence:   CI remains over budget or reports reduced coverage as success.

principles:             

causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               doc/E304.md
last_updated:           2026-07-30
source_event:           gromacs/2026.3 OHOS r7 seven 600-second mdrun timeouts resolved by propagating the no-measure policy to the direct 3D planner

authors:                2301_80739235
